      "description": "Watch Seattle Sounders FC vs Vancouver Whitecaps highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 17, 2026. The MLS clash between Seattle Sounders FC and Vancouver Whitecaps FC delivered a tactical masterclass that eventually exploded into life during the closing stages. Both teams showcased resilience in a match where squad depth proved to be the ultimate deciding factor. A Gritty Opening Period Played on August 17, 2026 , the match began with high energy but was quickly hampered by physical setbacks. The Vancouver Whitecaps were forced into an early change just 18 minutes in, as Jeevan Badwal made way for Rayan Elloumi . The trend continued for the Seattle Sounders later in the half when Jesus Ferreira was replaced by Sebastian Gomez in the 36th minute. These tactical adjustments dictated a cautious first half, with both sides heading into the tunnel with the deadlock still intact. Late Strikes Define the Outcome The second half saw the intensity ramp up significantly. Jackson Ragen picked up a yellow card in the 57th minute as the battle in midfield intensified. Managers turned to their benches, introducing the likes of Ryan Gauld and Tristan Blackmon to find a breakthrough. The deadlock was finally broken in the 77th minute when Emmanuel Sabbi provided a brilliant assist for Rayan Elloumi , who calmly slotted the ball home to give his side the lead. Building on that momentum, the match was put beyond doubt in the 82nd minute. Oliver Larraz turned provider, setting up Thomas Muller , who showed his trademark clinical edge to find the back of the net. Despite late yellow cards for Nouhou Tolo and Paul Rothrock , the Sounders maintained their composure. The final whistle at 90+6 marked the end of a captivating contest where the substitutes truly made the difference."
